exports[`each template's output > channel_ready, for clients: the snapshot 1`] = `
{
  "html": "<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark">
<meta name="supported-color-schemes" content="light dark">
<title>Phone is ready: one step left</title>
<style>@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  body, .hd-wrap { background: #0d1117 !important; color: #e6edf3 !important; }
  .hd-muted { color: #9da7b3 !important; }
  a { color: #8cc4ff !important; }
  a.hd-action { background: #e6edf3 !important; color: #0d1117 !important; }
}</style>
</head>
<body style="margin:0;padding:0;background:#ffffff;color:#1f2328;">
<span style="display:none;max-height:0;overflow:hidden;opacity:0;mso-hide:all;">Forward your main line to AYA and she starts answering.</span>
<div class="hd-wrap" style="max-width:560px;margin:0 auto;padding:24px 16px;font-family:-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.5;color:#1f2328;background:#ffffff;">
<p style="margin:0 0 16px;">AYA is ready to answer Radiance Med Spa&#39;s calls. One step is left, and it&#39;s yours: forward your main line to her, so the calls your team can&#39;t take reach her.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 4px;"><strong>Forward calls to:</strong> (512) 555-0142</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 16px;">The steps for Verizon:</p>
<ul style="margin:0 0 16px;padding-left:20px;"><li>On a Verizon home phone (Fios Digital Voice or a traditional line), forward calls when the line is busy or nobody answers. Verizon&#39;s star-code page gives *42 for this and its Calling Features User Guide gives *41: dial *42 and the number, and if a test call doesn&#39;t reach your assistant, dial *43, then *41 and the number instead: *425125550142</li><li>On a Verizon mobile line, forward the calls you don&#39;t answer within three or four rings, or can&#39;t take because you&#39;re on another call. Verizon documents this code only for those calls, not for a phone that is switched off, so leave the phone on while you&#39;re closed, or make the test call with it switched off: *715125550142</li><li>Your assistant gets a call only if nothing else answers it first. If an answering machine, a voicemail box or a closed-hours greeting on your line picks up before the forwarding does, the call stops there, so switch it off or set it to answer later than the forwarding.</li><li>Then test it: call your main number from a phone that isn&#39;t on the clinic&#39;s account and let it ring unanswered. Your assistant should answer. Test once while you&#39;re closed too.</li></ul>
<p style="margin:0 0 16px;">To undo it at any time:</p>
<ul style="margin:0 0 16px;padding-left:20px;"><li>Cancel busy and no-answer forwarding on a Verizon home phone: *43</li><li>If Verizon pointed your home phone&#39;s busy and no-answer forwarding at your assistant by service order instead, *43 doesn&#39;t undo it: ask Verizon to set it back to where it went before.</li><li>Cancel forwarding on a Verizon mobile line: *73</li></ul>
<p style="margin:16px 0 24px;"><a class="hd-action" href="https://app.healdesk.test/c/radiance-med-spa/setup?s=channels" style="display:inline-block;background:#1f2328;color:#ffffff;padding:10px 16px;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;">See the steps in healdesk</a></p>
<p style="margin:0 0 16px;">Forwarding is easier with someone on the line. Book a five-minute call and we&#39;ll do it with you.</p>
<p style="margin:16px 0 24px;"><a class="hd-action" href="https://app.healdesk.test/help/call" style="display:inline-block;background:#1f2328;color:#ffffff;padding:10px 16px;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;">Book a five-minute call</a></p>
<p style="margin:0 0 16px;">Questions? Reply to this email, or write to hello@healdesk.io. Or leave a message on (888) 555-0100: we reply the next business day. Please don&#39;t include client details.</p>
<hr style="border:none;border-top:1px solid #d0d7de;margin:24px 0 16px;">
<p class="hd-muted" style="margin:0 0 6px;color:#57606a;font-size:13px;">You&#39;re receiving this because this is the address on Radiance Med Spa&#39;s healdesk account.</p>
<p class="hd-muted" style="margin:0 0 6px;color:#57606a;font-size:13px;">Replies reach the healdesk team. Please leave out your clients&#39; details.</p>
<p class="hd-muted" style="margin:0 0 6px;color:#57606a;font-size:13px;">800 N King Street, Suite 304-1426, Wilmington, DE 19801, United States</p>
</div>
</body>
</html>",
  "preheader": "Forward your main line to AYA and she starts answering.",
  "subject": "Phone is ready: one step left",
  "text": "AYA is ready to answer Radiance Med Spa's calls. One step is left, and it's yours: forward your main line to her, so the calls your team can't take reach her.

Forward calls to: (512) 555-0142

The steps for Verizon:

- On a Verizon home phone (Fios Digital Voice or a traditional line), forward calls when the line is busy or nobody answers. Verizon's star-code page gives *42 for this and its Calling Features User Guide gives *41: dial *42 and the number, and if a test call doesn't reach your assistant, dial *43, then *41 and the number instead: *425125550142
- On a Verizon mobile line, forward the calls you don't answer within three or four rings, or can't take because you're on another call. Verizon documents this code only for those calls, not for a phone that is switched off, so leave the phone on while you're closed, or make the test call with it switched off: *715125550142
- Your assistant gets a call only if nothing else answers it first. If an answering machine, a voicemail box or a closed-hours greeting on your line picks up before the forwarding does, the call stops there, so switch it off or set it to answer later than the forwarding.
- Then test it: call your main number from a phone that isn't on the clinic's account and let it ring unanswered. Your assistant should answer. Test once while you're closed too.

To undo it at any time:

- Cancel busy and no-answer forwarding on a Verizon home phone: *43
- If Verizon pointed your home phone's busy and no-answer forwarding at your assistant by service order instead, *43 doesn't undo it: ask Verizon to set it back to where it went before.
- Cancel forwarding on a Verizon mobile line: *73

See the steps in healdesk: https://app.healdesk.test/c/radiance-med-spa/setup?s=channels

Forwarding is easier with someone on the line. Book a five-minute call and we'll do it with you.

Book a five-minute call: https://app.healdesk.test/help/call

Questions? Reply to this email, or write to hello@healdesk.io. Or leave a message on (888) 555-0100: we reply the next business day. Please don't include client details.

—
You're receiving this because this is the address on Radiance Med Spa's healdesk account.
Replies reach the healdesk team. Please leave out your clients' details.
800 N King Street, Suite 304-1426, Wilmington, DE 19801, United States
",
}
`;

