exports[`each template's output > steps_sent, for clients: the snapshot 1`] = `
{
  "html": "<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark">
<meta name="supported-color-schemes" content="light dark">
<title>Call forwarding steps from Radiance Med Spa</title>
<style>@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  body, .hd-wrap { background: #0d1117 !important; color: #e6edf3 !important; }
  .hd-muted { color: #9da7b3 !important; }
  a { color: #8cc4ff !important; }
  a.hd-action { background: #e6edf3 !important; color: #0d1117 !important; }
}</style>
</head>
<body style="margin:0;padding:0;background:#ffffff;color:#1f2328;">
<span style="display:none;max-height:0;overflow:hidden;opacity:0;mso-hide:all;">The steps to forward the practice&#39;s main line to AYA.</span>
<div class="hd-wrap" style="max-width:560px;margin:0 auto;padding:24px 16px;font-family:-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.5;color:#1f2328;background:#ffffff;">
<p style="margin:0 0 16px;">Radiance Med Spa asked us to send you these steps. They forward the practice&#39;s main line to AYA, its AI assistant from healdesk, so the calls the front desk can&#39;t take are answered. It&#39;s done by following the steps below for the practice&#39;s kind of line, dialling each code from the main line itself.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 4px;"><strong>Forward calls to:</strong> (512) 555-0142</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 16px;">The steps for AT&amp;T:</p>
<ul style="margin:0 0 16px;padding-left:20px;"><li>On AT&amp;T Phone, AT&amp;T&#39;s digital home and business service, forward calls when the line is busy, pressing # after the number: *905125550142#</li><li>On AT&amp;T Phone, forward calls nobody answers, pressing # after the number: *925125550142#</li><li>On AT&amp;T Phone, forward calls while service on your line is disrupted (AT&amp;T&#39;s Safe Call Forwarding): *3725125550142#</li><li>On a traditional AT&amp;T landline, busy and no-answer forwarding has no code: call AT&amp;T on 800.288.2020 and ask for Call Forwarding - Busy Line and Call Forwarding - Don&#39;t Answer, to: +15125550142</li><li>On an AT&amp;T mobile line, AT&amp;T lets forwarding be changed only from the phone itself and gives no code for busy or unanswered calls: in the phone&#39;s own call-forwarding settings, if they offer forwarding when busy, unanswered or unreachable (AT&amp;T&#39;s device help for your phone shows where; some phones offer only all-call forwarding), forward those calls to: +15125550142</li><li>Your assistant gets a call only if nothing else answers it first. If an answering machine, a voicemail box or a closed-hours greeting on your line picks up before the forwarding does, the call stops there, so switch it off or set it to answer later than the forwarding.</li><li>Then test it: call your main number from a phone that isn&#39;t on the clinic&#39;s account and let it ring unanswered. Your assistant should answer. Test once while you&#39;re closed too.</li></ul>
<p style="margin:0 0 16px;">To undo it at any time:</p>
<ul style="margin:0 0 16px;padding-left:20px;"><li>Cancel busy forwarding on AT&amp;T Phone: *91#</li><li>Cancel no-answer forwarding on AT&amp;T Phone: *93#</li><li>Cancel Safe Call Forwarding on AT&amp;T Phone: *373#</li><li>On AT&amp;T Phone, those codes don&#39;t bring back AT&amp;T voicemail for missed calls. To send unanswered and busy calls to voicemail again on AT&amp;T Phone for Business, sign in to your AT&amp;T account, open Voicemail Settings and set No Answer and Busy Call Forwarding to Forward to Voice Mail; on AT&amp;T Phone at home, ask AT&amp;T to set them back to voicemail.</li><li>On a traditional AT&amp;T landline, call AT&amp;T on 800.288.2020 to remove busy and no-answer forwarding, or to set it back to your voicemail if that&#39;s where it went before.</li><li>On an AT&amp;T mobile line, turn the forwarding off in the phone&#39;s own call-forwarding settings (AT&amp;T lets forwarding be changed only from the phone itself).</li></ul>
<p style="margin:0 0 16px;">Easier with someone on the line? Book a five-minute call and we&#39;ll do it with you.</p>
<p style="margin:16px 0 24px;"><a class="hd-action" href="https://app.healdesk.test/help/call" style="display:inline-block;background:#1f2328;color:#ffffff;padding:10px 16px;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;">Book a five-minute call</a></p>
<p style="margin:0 0 16px;">Questions? Reply to this email and a person at healdesk answers.</p>
<hr style="border:none;border-top:1px solid #d0d7de;margin:24px 0 16px;">
<p class="hd-muted" style="margin:0 0 6px;color:#57606a;font-size:13px;">You&#39;re receiving this because someone at Radiance Med Spa asked us to send it to this address.</p>
<p class="hd-muted" style="margin:0 0 6px;color:#57606a;font-size:13px;">Replies reach the healdesk team. Please leave out your clients&#39; details.</p>
<p class="hd-muted" style="margin:0 0 6px;color:#57606a;font-size:13px;">Stop these emails: <a href="https://app.healdesk.test/email/stop/MGMxZDJlM2YtMDAwMC00MDAwLTgwMDAtMDAwMDAwMDAwMDAwOnN0ZXBzOjBiMWMyZDNlLTRmNTAtNDYxNy04ODk5LWFhYmJjY2RkZWVmZg.qourRwxBgFS1PaE65qR5Rou6y0SU5viMryvA999pXHA">https://app.healdesk.test/email/stop/MGMxZDJlM2YtMDAwMC00MDAwLTgwMDAtMDAwMDAwMDAwMDAwOnN0ZXBzOjBiMWMyZDNlLTRmNTAtNDYxNy04ODk5LWFhYmJjY2RkZWVmZg.qourRwxBgFS1PaE65qR5Rou6y0SU5viMryvA999pXHA</a></p>
<p class="hd-muted" style="margin:0 0 6px;color:#57606a;font-size:13px;">800 N King Street, Suite 304-1426, Wilmington, DE 19801, United States</p>
</div>
</body>
</html>",
  "preheader": "The steps to forward the practice's main line to AYA.",
  "subject": "Call forwarding steps from Radiance Med Spa",
  "text": "Radiance Med Spa asked us to send you these steps. They forward the practice's main line to AYA, its AI assistant from healdesk, so the calls the front desk can't take are answered. It's done by following the steps below for the practice's kind of line, dialling each code from the main line itself.

Forward calls to: (512) 555-0142

The steps for AT&T:

- On AT&T Phone, AT&T's digital home and business service, forward calls when the line is busy, pressing # after the number: *905125550142#
- On AT&T Phone, forward calls nobody answers, pressing # after the number: *925125550142#
- On AT&T Phone, forward calls while service on your line is disrupted (AT&T's Safe Call Forwarding): *3725125550142#
- On a traditional AT&T landline, busy and no-answer forwarding has no code: call AT&T on 800.288.2020 and ask for Call Forwarding - Busy Line and Call Forwarding - Don't Answer, to: +15125550142
- On an AT&T mobile line, AT&T lets forwarding be changed only from the phone itself and gives no code for busy or unanswered calls: in the phone's own call-forwarding settings, if they offer forwarding when busy, unanswered or unreachable (AT&T's device help for your phone shows where; some phones offer only all-call forwarding), forward those calls to: +15125550142
- Your assistant gets a call only if nothing else answers it first. If an answering machine, a voicemail box or a closed-hours greeting on your line picks up before the forwarding does, the call stops there, so switch it off or set it to answer later than the forwarding.
- Then test it: call your main number from a phone that isn't on the clinic's account and let it ring unanswered. Your assistant should answer. Test once while you're closed too.

To undo it at any time:

- Cancel busy forwarding on AT&T Phone: *91#
- Cancel no-answer forwarding on AT&T Phone: *93#
- Cancel Safe Call Forwarding on AT&T Phone: *373#
- On AT&T Phone, those codes don't bring back AT&T voicemail for missed calls. To send unanswered and busy calls to voicemail again on AT&T Phone for Business, sign in to your AT&T account, open Voicemail Settings and set No Answer and Busy Call Forwarding to Forward to Voice Mail; on AT&T Phone at home, ask AT&T to set them back to voicemail.
- On a traditional AT&T landline, call AT&T on 800.288.2020 to remove busy and no-answer forwarding, or to set it back to your voicemail if that's where it went before.
- On an AT&T mobile line, turn the forwarding off in the phone's own call-forwarding settings (AT&T lets forwarding be changed only from the phone itself).

Easier with someone on the line? Book a five-minute call and we'll do it with you.

Book a five-minute call: https://app.healdesk.test/help/call

Questions? Reply to this email and a person at healdesk answers.

—
You're receiving this because someone at Radiance Med Spa asked us to send it to this address.
Replies reach the healdesk team. Please leave out your clients' details.
