exports[`ops alerts beyond the fixture > the DMARC review reminder: the snapshot 1`] = `
{
  "html": "<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark">
<meta name="supported-color-schemes" content="light dark">
<title>healdesk ops: Time to review the DMARC reports</title>
<style>@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  body, .hd-wrap { background: #0d1117 !important; color: #e6edf3 !important; }
  .hd-muted { color: #9da7b3 !important; }
  a { color: #8cc4ff !important; }
  a.hd-action { background: #e6edf3 !important; color: #0d1117 !important; }
}</style>
</head>
<body style="margin:0;padding:0;background:#ffffff;color:#1f2328;">
<span style="display:none;max-height:0;overflow:hidden;opacity:0;mso-hide:all;">FYI: Two weeks of DMARC reports should be in: time to decide on tightening healdesk.io&#39;s record</span>
<div class="hd-wrap" style="max-width:560px;margin:0 auto;padding:24px 16px;font-family:-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.5;color:#1f2328;background:#ffffff;">
<p style="margin:0 0 8px;"><span style="display:inline-block;background:#57606a;color:#ffffff;font-size:13px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.08em;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:4px;">FYI</span></p>
<p style="margin:0 0 16px;font-size:20px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;">Two weeks of DMARC reports should be in: time to decide on tightening healdesk.io&#39;s record</p>
<div style="margin:0 0 20px;padding:12px 14px;background:#fff8c5;color:#1f2328;border:1px solid #d4a72c;border-radius:6px;"><p style="margin:0 0 6px;color:#1f2328;"><strong>Do this first</strong></p><p style="margin:0;color:#1f2328;">Read healdesk.io&#39;s DMARC aggregate reports from <mark style="background:#ffd54f;color:#1f2328;padding:0 2px;">6 Oct</mark> on, in the mailbox named after rua= in the DMARC record in Cloudflare. The dmarc-review row on the <strong><u>Jobs page</u></strong> under System names the same first-sending day in its note, on the run that raised this alert.</p></div>
<hr style="border:none;border-top:1px solid #d0d7de;margin:24px 0 12px;">
<p class="hd-muted" style="margin:0 0 12px;color:#57606a;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.08em;text-transform:uppercase;">More detail</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 16px;">Resend has been sending as healdesk.io for 14 days or more, since <mark style="background:#fff3a3;color:#1f2328;padding:0 2px;">6 Oct</mark> or earlier, where the reports to read begin, and the record stays at report-only until someone changes it; this alert does not read it.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 4px;"><strong>Raised:</strong> 6 Oct</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 16px;"><strong>Why it matters:</strong> Until the record says quarantine, anyone can send mail as hello@ and inboxes will accept it. Tightening it blind could block our own mail, so the reports are read first.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 16px;"><strong>Then:</strong><br>2. Check the reports show only our own senders as healdesk.io: Resend, Amazon&#39;s email service (our transcripts) and the owner&#39;s own mail. The <strong><u>Map page</u></strong> under System lists the first two. Find out what anything else is before going on; do not touch the record while an unknown sender shows.<br>3. Ask the owner to change healdesk.io&#39;s DMARC record from p=none to p=quarantine in Cloudflare, which holds healdesk.io&#39;s addresses; the <strong><u>Map page</u></strong> under System lists it, and only the owner has the Cloudflare sign-in. You are done when the record reads p=quarantine. This alert is raised once only.</p>
<p class="hd-muted" style="margin:16px 0 0;color:#57606a;font-size:13px;">Alert code: dmarc_review_due</p>
<hr style="border:none;border-top:1px solid #d0d7de;margin:24px 0 16px;">
<p class="hd-muted" style="margin:0 0 6px;color:#57606a;font-size:13px;">You&#39;re receiving this because this address is set as healdesk&#39;s ops alert address.</p>
<p class="hd-muted" style="margin:0 0 6px;color:#57606a;font-size:13px;">Replies reach the healdesk team. Please leave out patient details.</p>
<p class="hd-muted" style="margin:0 0 6px;color:#57606a;font-size:13px;">800 N King Street, Suite 304-1426, Wilmington, DE 19801, United States</p>
</div>
</body>
</html>",
  "preheader": "FYI: Two weeks of DMARC reports should be in: time to decide on tightening healdesk.io's record",
  "subject": "healdesk ops: Time to review the DMARC reports",
  "text": "FYI: Two weeks of DMARC reports should be in: time to decide on tightening healdesk.io's record

DO THIS FIRST: Read healdesk.io's DMARC aggregate reports from 6 Oct on, in the mailbox named after rua= in the DMARC record in Cloudflare. The dmarc-review row on the Jobs page under System names the same first-sending day in its note, on the run that raised this alert.

MORE DETAIL

Resend has been sending as healdesk.io for 14 days or more, since 6 Oct or earlier, where the reports to read begin, and the record stays at report-only until someone changes it; this alert does not read it.

Raised: 6 Oct

WHY IT MATTERS: Until the record says quarantine, anyone can send mail as hello@ and inboxes will accept it. Tightening it blind could block our own mail, so the reports are read first.

THEN:
2. Check the reports show only our own senders as healdesk.io: Resend, Amazon's email service (our transcripts) and the owner's own mail. The Map page under System lists the first two. Find out what anything else is before going on; do not touch the record while an unknown sender shows.
3. Ask the owner to change healdesk.io's DMARC record from p=none to p=quarantine in Cloudflare, which holds healdesk.io's addresses; the Map page under System lists it, and only the owner has the Cloudflare sign-in. You are done when the record reads p=quarantine. This alert is raised once only.

Alert code: dmarc_review_due

—
You're receiving this because this address is set as healdesk's ops alert address.
Replies reach the healdesk team. Please leave out patient details.
800 N King Street, Suite 304-1426, Wilmington, DE 19801, United States
",
}
`;

